# AI providers (pick one). Keys stay in process env / local settings only —
# never written into ZIP packages, extension storage, or bridge logs.
#
# Free / local (preferred for demos — no paid credits):
#   1) Install Ollama or LM Studio, pull/load a model, leave the server running
#   2) Prefer exact tags: smollm2:135m or llama3.2:latest (never strip :tag)
#   3) Or leave daemon up — bridge auto-detects Ollama (:11434) / LM Studio (:1234)
# TABHANDOFF_AI_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:latest
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# TABHANDOFF_AI_PROVIDER=lmstudio
# LMSTUDIO_MODEL=local-model
# LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1
#
# OpenAI-compatible cloud (founder-owned key — never paste into the extension):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#
# Groq (OpenAI-compatible free-tier friendly):
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
#
# Anthropic:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# Optional override for receipt/job/AI-task store (default: ~/.tabhandoff)
# TABHANDOFF_HOME=
